// The hosted voice agent's public ElevenLabs ID, for agent connection calls
// (HappyCore CallAgent). Never committed: a public ID lets anyone start a
// conversation billed to its owner. Set it in Call.local.xcconfig next to
// this file (ignored by git) or on the build's command line:
//     HAPPY_CALL_AGENT_V3_ID = agent_...
// Named for the tools this code calls (v3: listConversations,
// readConversation, message, navigate), so an older agent's ID, set under
// the old HAPPY_CALL_AGENT_ID, never reaches it. Without it, the voice
// button says voice isn't set up.
HAPPY_CALL_AGENT_V3_ID =

// RevenueCat's public Apple app key, for voice's subscription (pro). The
// same key the Expo app gets from EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUE_CAT_APPLE, which is
// where it comes from here too: set that in the build's environment, or
// override this in Call.local.xcconfig. Without it voice sells nothing.
HAPPY_REVENUE_CAT_APPLE_KEY = $(EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUE_CAT_APPLE)
#include? "Call.local.xcconfig"
